# =============================================================================
#  R8 / ProGuard — :app
#
#  RULE #1: DO NOT ADD `-keep class <package>.** { *; }` (nor `-keep class ** { *; }`).
#
#  Such a rule forbids R8 to remove, rename AND optimize a whole package tree. On a real app
#  eleven of them produced a 36.8 MB DEX and Play's "App optimization: Low" (18/18/19%).
#  Enforced by ProguardRulesTest (the only allowed wide keeps are listed there, with reasons).
#
#  Something breaks only in release? Do NOT widen a keep. Find the exact class/member:
#    build/outputs/mapping/<variant>/usage.txt          — what R8 removed
#    build/outputs/mapping/<variant>/mapping.txt        — what it renamed, and to what
#    build/outputs/mapping/<variant>/seeds.txt          — what keep rules currently hold
#    build/outputs/mapping/<variant>/configuration.txt  — final config incl. library consumer rules
#  and add the narrowest rule below, with a comment: what reads it by name, where, what broke.
# =============================================================================

# ── Readable stack traces ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# mapping.txt of every released variant is archived (named by versionName + versionCode)
# and uploaded to the crash reporter. Cheap (~0.1–0.2 MB).
-keepattributes SourceFile,LineNumberTable
-renamesourcefileattribute SourceFile

# ── kotlinx.serialization (R8 full mode) ─────────────────────────────────────
# Annotations so the -if rules can see @Serializable; Signature for generic types.
# Official rules from the kotlinx.serialization README ("Android").
-keepattributes Signature
-keepattributes RuntimeVisibleAnnotations,RuntimeVisibleParameterAnnotations,AnnotationDefault
-if @kotlinx.serialization.Serializable class **
-keepclassmembers class <1> {
    static <1>$Companion Companion;
}
-if @kotlinx.serialization.Serializable class ** {
    static **$* *;
}
-keepclassmembers class <2>$<3> {
    kotlinx.serialization.KSerializer serializer(...);
}
-if @kotlinx.serialization.Serializable class ** {
    public static ** INSTANCE;
}
-keepclassmembers class <1> {
    public static <1> INSTANCE;
    kotlinx.serialization.KSerializer serializer(...);
}
# A @Serializable class without explicit @SerialName is serialized under its FQCN; stored files
# must stay readable across app versions. -keepnames still lets R8 drop unused classes.
-keepnames @kotlinx.serialization.Serializable class com.example.app.**

# ── Room ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Room.databaseBuilder(ctx, AppDatabase::class.java, …) loads "<FQCN>_Impl" by name.
-keep class * extends androidx.room.RoomDatabase { <init>(); }

# ── protobuf-lite (DataStore / Tink) ─────────────────────────────────────────
# protobuf-lite reads generated message fields BY NAME. Renaming them loses settings (DataStore)
# or makes EncryptedSharedPreferences unreadable (Tink) — only on UPDATE, never on fresh install.
# Fields only: the classes themselves may still be removed and renamed.
-keepclassmembers class * extends androidx.datastore.preferences.protobuf.GeneratedMessageLite {
    <fields>;
}
-keepclassmembers class * extends com.google.crypto.tink.shaded.protobuf.GeneratedMessageLite {
    <fields>;
}

# ── JNI ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The one justified wide keep: native code calls these Java classes/methods by name.
# Listed in ProguardRulesTest.KNOWN_WIDE_KEEPS with this reason. Measure its cost (classes kept).
-keep class com.example.nativelib.** { *; }

# ── Class names used as data ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Screen analytics send `screen::class.simpleName`; without this the dashboard shows "a", "b".
-keepnames class * implements com.example.app.navigation.Screen

# ── -dontwarn: optional dependencies absent on Android ───────────────────────
# ONLY lines copied from build/outputs/mapping/<variant>/missing_rules.txt, each with its origin.
# Never -keep here.

# Tink / errorprone annotations (transitive of androidx.security:security-crypto)
-dontwarn javax.annotation.**
-dontwarn com.google.errorprone.annotations.**

# ── Deliberately ABSENT ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  kotlin.** / kotlinx.**      — stdlib needs no keep; coroutines ship consumer rules.
#  androidx.compose.**         — R8-compatible; a wide keep here kept ~11 400 icon classes.
#  androidx.room.** (whole)    — room-runtime ships consumer rules; only the _Impl lookup above.
#  org.koin.**                 — resolves by KClass, not by string.
#  com.example.app.**          — our own code must shrink and obfuscate.
#  <analytics/crash SDK>       — ships its own consumer rules.
